<PageTitle>Blazor TextBox, Numeric TextBox and TextArea — FlexCore</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Text inputs" Category="Components" CategoryHref="components"
                   ControlName="TextBoxControl · NumericTextBoxControl · TextAreaControl · MaskedTextBoxControl · PasswordControl"
                   Tagline="Collect names, numbers, notes, phone numbers and passwords, bound two ways to your model."
                   SourcePath="TextBoxControl.razor; NumericTextBoxControl.razor; TextAreaControl.razor; MaskedTextBoxControl.razor; MaskPattern.cs; PasswordControl.razor">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>TextBoxControl</code> is a Blazor text box for a line of text, updated on every keystroke with <code>UpdateOnInput</code> or once users leave the field. Use <code>NumericTextBoxControl</code> for counts and amounts that must stay in range, <code>TextAreaControl</code> for notes with a character limit and spell checking, <code>MaskedTextBoxControl</code> for entries with a fixed format such as a phone number, and <code>PasswordControl</code> for passwords with a reveal button. All five bind with <code>&#64;bind-Value</code>.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="details" Title="Traveler details" RazorCode="@Code.Details" CSharpCode="@Code.DetailsCs">
            <Description><p>Type in each field and watch the card: the name on the tag follows every keystroke and has a clear button, the email lands when you leave the box, the traveler count stays between 1 and 12, and Budget refuses anything under $250 a head, with a warning when more travelers leave an accepted budget below that.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="ti">
                    <div class="details">
                        <label class="field">
                            <span class="field-label">Lead traveler</span>
                            <TextBoxControl @bind-Value="_name" UpdateOnInput="true" ShowClearButton="true"
                                            Placeholder="Full name as on the passport" MaxLength="40" CssClass="text-field" />
                        </label>
                        <label class="field">
                            <span class="field-label">Email</span>
                            <TextBoxControl @bind-Value="_email" InputType="email"
                                            Placeholder="name@example.com" MaxLength="80" CssClass="text-field" />
                        </label>
                        <label class="field">
                            <span class="field-label">Travelers (1 to 12)</span>
                            <NumericTextBoxControl TValue="int" @bind-Value="_travelers" Min="1" Max="12" Width="90px" />
                        </label>
                        <label class="field">
                            <span class="field-label">Budget in dollars, steps of 50</span>
                            <NumericTextBoxControl TValue="decimal" Value="_budget" ValueChange="CheckBudget"
                                                   Format="C2" Step="50" Min="0" Width="140px" />
                        </label>
                    </div>
                    <div class="tag-preview" role="status">
                        <span class="tag-name">@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_name) ? "NO NAME YET" : _name.ToUpperInvariant())</span>
                        <span><strong>@Trip.Name</strong>, @Trip.Nights nights, @TravelerCount</span>
                        <span>Confirmation goes to @(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_email) ? "nobody yet" : _email)</span>
                        <span>Budget @_budget.ToString("$#,##0") (@((_budget / _travelers).ToString("$#,##0")) a head)</span>
                    </div>
                    <p class="warn" role="status">@(_budgetNote ?? LowBudget)</p>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="notes" Title="Notes with a limit" RazorCode="@Code.Notes" CSharpCode="@Code.NotesCs">
            <Description><p>Type up to 200 characters; each button inserts a stock phrase at the caret, and is refused when it would pass the limit. The switch turns on the control's own context menu.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="ti">
                    <div class="notes">
                        <label class="field">
                            <span class="field-label">Booking note for @Trip.Name</span>
                            <Fx.ControlKit.TextAreaControl @ref="_noteBox" @bind-Value="_note" UpdateOnInput="true" MaxLength="NoteLimit" Rows="5"
                                                           SpellCheck="true" Placeholder="Dietary needs, room requests, arrival times"
                                                           UseClassicContextMenu="_classicMenu" ContextMenuItems="TextContextMenuItems.Editing" />
                        </label>
                        <div class="note-bar">
                            <span class="count @(NoteLimit - NoteLength <= 20 ? "near" : null)">@NoteLength / @NoteLimit characters</span>
                            @foreach (var phrase in Phrases)
                            {
                                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="() => Insert(phrase)">@phrase</ButtonControl>
                            }
                            <SwitchControl @bind-Checked="_classicMenu" Label="Classic context menu" />
                        </div>
                        <p class="warn" role="status">@_noteStatus</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Id="portal" Title="A phone mask and a password" RazorCode="@Code.Portal" CSharpCode="@Code.PortalCs">
            <Description><p>Set up the lead traveler's portal account: the mobile number is formatted and checked against its <code>Mask</code> when you leave the box, and the password box shows each character for a moment and has an eye to reveal it; the page checks off the rules below it as you type. <code>OnChange</code> reports only numbers the mask accepts, so Create account checks the number again with <code>CommitAsync</code>.</p></Description>
            <Demo>
                <div class="ti">
                    <div class="details">
                        <label class="field">
                            <span class="field-label">Mobile number</span>
                            <MaskedTextBoxControl @ref="_mask" @bind-Value="_phone" Mask="000-000-0000" Required="true" Placeholder="206-555-0142" AriaLabel="Mobile number" OnChange="PhoneSet" />
                        </label>
                        <label class="field">
                            <span class="field-label">Password</span>
                            <PasswordControl @bind-Value="_password" RevealLastTypedCharacter="true" PasswordRevealDurationMs="800" MaxLength="40" Width="100%"
                                             Placeholder="At least 8 characters" CssClass="text-field" aria-label="Password" />
                        </label>
                    </div>
                    <ul class="rules">
                        <li class="@(LongEnough ? "ok" : null)">8 characters or more</li>
                        <li class="@(HasDigit ? "ok" : null)">a digit</li>
                        <li class="@(HasUpper ? "ok" : null)">a capital letter</li>
                    </ul>
                    <div class="note-bar">
                        <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-primary btn-sm" Disabled="@(!CanCreate)" OnClick="CreateAccount">Create account</ButtonControl>
                        <span class="warn" role="status">@_portal</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <DocSections>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textboxcontrol-parameters" Title="TextBoxControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextBox.Length, "parameters")' Open="true">
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="TextBoxControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.TextBox" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textboxcontrol-password-parameters" Title="TextBoxControl password parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Password.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="TextBoxControl password parameters" Rows="Vocab.Password" />
                <p>These apply when <code>InputType="password"</code> on a single-line box. <code>PasswordControl</code> wraps a <code>TextBoxControl</code> for password fields; its own members are in the next table.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-passwordcontrol-parameters" Title="PasswordControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.PasswordCtl.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="PasswordControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.PasswordCtl" />
                <p><code>ValueChanged</code> and <code>ReplacementChanged</code> carry the text, on every keystroke by default. Methods: <code>FocusAsync()</code>, and <code>FlushClientBufferedValueAsync()</code>, which sends a client-buffered draft before you validate or save.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textboxcontrol-events" Title="TextBoxControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextBoxEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="TextBoxControl events" Rows="Vocab.TextBoxEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textboxcontrol-methods" Title="TextBoxControl methods" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextBoxMethods.Length, "methods")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Methods" Title="TextBoxControl methods" Rows="Vocab.TextBoxMethods" />
                <p><code>CommitClientBufferedTypingAsync</code> and <code>OnPasteTruncatedAsync</code> are public only so the control's script can call them.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-numerictextboxcontrol-parameters" Title="NumericTextBoxControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.Numeric.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="NumericTextBoxControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.Numeric" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-numerictextboxcontrol-events" Title="NumericTextBoxControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.NumericEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="NumericTextBoxControl events" Rows="Vocab.NumericEvents" />
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-numericchangeeventargs" Title="NumericChangeEventArgs" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.NumericArgs.Length, "properties")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Properties" Title="NumericChangeEventArgs" Rows="Vocab.NumericArgs" />
                <p>The class is nested inside the control, so a handler names it in full: <code>NumericTextBoxControl&lt;decimal&gt;.NumericChangeEventArgs&lt;decimal&gt;</code>, as the budget example does.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textareacontrol-parameters" Title="TextAreaControl parameters" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextArea.Length, "parameters")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Parameters" Title="TextAreaControl parameters" Rows="Vocab.TextArea" />
                <p>A second, simpler <code>TextAreaControl</code> lives in <code>Fx.ControlKit.Editor</code>: a plain rounded textarea that reports every keystroke unless <code>BindOnChange</code> is set, adds <code>Cols</code>, <code>ReadOnly</code> and <code>Style</code>, and has no context menu, scroll-bar modes, typing modes or methods. With both namespaces imported, write the full name, as this page does with <code>Fx.ControlKit.TextAreaControl</code>.</p>
            </DocSection>
            <DocSection Id="doc-textareacontrol-events" Title="TextAreaControl events" Count='@DocSection.Label(Vocab.TextAreaEvents.Length, "events")'>
                <ApiTable Kind="ApiKind.Events" Title="TextAreaControl events" Rows="Vocab.TextAreaEvents" />
            </DocSection>
